# Findings of the image scan (tools/image_scan.py, NFR-09) that are accepted
# for now. Each entry is a vulnerability ID with an expiry date, after which
# trivy reports it again, and the comment line directly above it says why it
# is accepted; the scan refuses an entry without either. For example:
#
#   # Only in the builder stage's uv, which the runtime image does not contain.
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Every entry below was re-checked against the current advisories on
# 2026-11-07 (#286), the krb5-libs entries of cAdvisor added on 2026-11-11.
# The expiry, 2027-01-31, lies after the final
# presentation of 2026-12-15 and the end of the course, so the scan cannot
# turn main red while the project is graded; it is the date of the next
# review that the scan forces.

# node-exporter v1.12.1 and cAdvisor v0.60.6 (deploy/compose.yaml), still the
# newest releases on 2026-11-07, are built with Go and libraries older than
# these fixes. Both publish no port and answer only Prometheus and their
# healthcheck inside the Compose network (docs/docs/monitoring.md). Accepted
# until a release with the fixes, which Dependabot proposes.
# crypto/x509 intermediate certificates (Go stdlib): the exporters open no TLS connection; in Grafana's bundled plugins, see below.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2027-01-31
# encoding/asn1 recursion (Go stdlib): the exporters parse no ASN.1 from a client, as they serve no TLS.
CVE-2026-33818 exp:2027-01-31
# x/net/idna Punycode labels (Go stdlib): the exporters resolve only the Compose service names.
CVE-2026-39821 exp:2027-01-31
# x/net/dns/dnsmessage parsing (Go stdlib): the only DNS server they ask is Docker's embedded one.
CVE-2026-46600 exp:2027-01-31
# x/text Nickname profile: reached through IDNA host names, which the exporters never get from a client.
CVE-2026-56851 exp:2027-01-31
# net/http unencrypted HTTP/2 (Go stdlib): the exporters serve HTTP/1.1, and only to Prometheus in the Compose network.
CVE-2026-56853 exp:2027-01-31
# x/crypto/ssh source-address restrictions: neither exporter runs an SSH server.
CVE-2026-56854 exp:2027-01-31
# html/template (Go stdlib): the pages the exporters render are reached only from inside the Compose network.
CVE-2026-56858 exp:2027-01-31
# encoding/xml recursion (Go stdlib): the exporters decode no XML from a client.
CVE-2026-56859 exp:2027-01-31
# net/url path resolution (Go stdlib): only Prometheus and the healthcheck send the exporters a URL, from inside the Compose network.
CVE-2026-56860 exp:2027-01-31
# crypto/tls KeyUpdate (Go stdlib): the exporters serve and open no TLS connection.
CVE-2026-56862 exp:2027-01-31
# klauspost/compress dictionaries in cAdvisor: it decompresses nothing a client sends.
CVE-2026-63209 exp:2027-01-31
# net/http Range headers (Go stdlib): only Prometheus and the healthcheck reach the exporters, from inside the Compose network; in Grafana's bundled plugins, see below.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2027-01-31
# net/http HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames (Go stdlib, x/net): the exporters serve no HTTP/2 and only inside the Compose network; in Grafana's bundled plugins, see below.
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2027-01-31
# gRPC-Go DATA frames in cAdvisor: it serves no gRPC, and its containerd client has no socket mounted to reach.
CVE-2026-84304 exp:2027-01-31
# gRPC-Go malformed requests in cAdvisor: it serves no gRPC.
CVE-2026-84445 exp:2027-01-31
# crypto/tls ECH extensions (Go stdlib): the exporters serve and open no TLS connection; in Grafana's bundled plugins, see below.
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2027-01-31
# gRPC-Go xDS RBAC in cAdvisor: it uses no xDS and serves no gRPC.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf exp:2027-01-31

# Grafana 13.3.0 (deploy/compose.yaml), still the newest release on
# 2026-11-07: apart from CVE-2026-78661 (x/net/html, see below), every HIGH
# finding is in a backend binary of a data source plugin it bundles, none in
# Grafana's own binary or in its Prometheus plugin
# (gpx_grafana-prometheus-datasource), the one plugin process that runs. The Go
# stdlib findings CVE-2026-111943, CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669 and
# CVE-2026-97031 above match nine of them as well: the Jaeger, Loki, MSSQL,
# MySQL, CloudWatch, InfluxDB, PostgreSQL, OpenTSDB and Pyroscope plugins; the
# two entries below match the Tempo plugin alone. compose.yaml turns every one
# of those plugins off (GF_PLUGINS_DISABLE_PLUGINS), so their binaries never
# run, which the integration suite checks
# (tests/integration/test_deployed_grafana.py); the stack provisions Prometheus
# alone, and Grafana is reachable only through the SSH tunnel
# (docs/docs/monitoring.md#grafana). The image's slim variant bundles none of
# these plugins, but none of Prometheus either. Accepted until a Grafana release
# with the fixes.
# github.com/grafana/tempo in the bundled Tempo plugin, fixed in Tempo 2.8.4: the plugin is off.
CVE-2026-21728 exp:2027-01-31
# github.com/grafana/tempo in the bundled Tempo plugin, fixed in Tempo 2.10.3: the plugin is off.
CVE-2026-28377 exp:2027-01-31

# golang.org/x/net/html before 0.62.0 in every Go binary of the stack
# (deploy/compose.yaml): no release of Prometheus (v3.16.0 included),
# Alertmanager, node-exporter, cAdvisor or Grafana is built with 0.62.0 on
# 2026-11-07. `govulncheck -mode=binary` (GO-2026-6860) finds the html package
# in none of prometheus, promtool, alertmanager, amtool, node_exporter and
# cadvisor, only the module, and in Grafana's own binary the package but none of
# the affected functions. Of Grafana's bundled plugins, which link html.Parse,
# only the Prometheus plugin runs (see Grafana's entries above), and its input
# comes from the stack's own Prometheus and from users who reach Grafana
# through the SSH tunnel. Accepted until releases with the fix.
# Quadratic time parsing crafted HTML, a denial of service: no binary that runs parses HTML a stranger sends.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2027-01-31

# musl and zlib in the Alpine layers of nginx-unprivileged:1.30-alpine-slim and
# cAdvisor v0.60.6 (deploy/compose.yaml): Alpine has the fixes, but no image of
# either tag is rebuilt with them on 2026-11-07, and building our own nginx
# image was ruled out (EDN-95).
# musl's regcomp() with an untrusted regular expression: nginx compiles its regular expressions, all from its own configuration, with PCRE2 and imports no regcomp; neither cadvisor nor its libpfm imports it.
CVE-2026-107891 exp:2027-01-31
# zlib's gzwrite()/gzprintf() path: nginx imports zlib's deflate and inflate but no gz* function, cadvisor links no zlib. The API and monitoring images take the fixed zlib1g (Dockerfile), and CVE-2026-76844, fixed by the same package and not accepted, still fails the scan if zlib1g regresses there.
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2027-01-31

# krb5-libs 1.22.1-r0 in the Alpine layer of cAdvisor v0.60.6
# (deploy/compose.yaml): Alpine ships the fix in 1.22.3-r0, but no image of the
# tag is rebuilt with it on 2026-11-11. Nothing that runs in the container loads
# Kerberos: cadvisor links only libpfm and musl, the healthcheck is busybox
# wget, and krb5-libs is there only for libtirpc, which only the ZFS tools load
# (through libnvpair). cadvisor runs `zfs` only when it sees /dev/zfs or, with
# the `disk` metric on, when Docker uses the zfs storage driver; neither holds
# here (the container gets no device, --enable_metrics leaves `disk` out, and
# the VM runs overlay2), and even then `zfs` would load the libraries without
# network input. The image has no KDC or kadmind, which most of these findings
# are in. Accepted until a rebuilt image, which Dependabot proposes.
# KDC ASN.1 decoder read overrun: the image runs no KDC, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-107364 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind RPCSEC_GSS buffer decode leak: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112315 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind xdr_krb5_tl_data() decode leak: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112316 exp:2027-01-31
# KDC keytab key decryption leak: the image runs no KDC, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112317 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind null policy name dereference: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112318 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind unbounded RPC XDR allocation: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112319 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind GSS-RPC auth flavor switching leak: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112320 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT error path leak: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112321 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind AUTH_GSSAPI client state cleanup: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112322 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind failed AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT requests: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-112323 exp:2027-01-31
# kadmind request alteration and disclosure: the image runs no kadmind, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-118380 exp:2027-01-31
# KDC quadratic ASN.1 SEQUENCE OF decoding: the image runs no KDC, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-119079 exp:2027-01-31
# NegoEx NULL dereference in gss_accept_sec_context(): nothing in the image loads krb5 or accepts a GSS token.
CVE-2026-40355 exp:2027-01-31
# NegoEx integer underflow in gss_accept_sec_context(): nothing in the image loads krb5 or accepts a GSS token.
CVE-2026-40356 exp:2027-01-31
# CAMMAC authentication indicator bypass: nothing in the image loads krb5 or accepts a Kerberos ticket.
CVE-2026-71199 exp:2027-01-31
# KDC PKINIT pre-auth NULL dereference: the image runs no KDC, and nothing in it loads krb5.
CVE-2026-71200 exp:2027-01-31

# transformers 4.57.6 in the monitoring image (monitoring/Dockerfile): Alibi
# Detect 0.13 requires transformers<5 and imports it when it is imported, but
# the drift job never loads, saves or downloads a model, tokenizer or
# configuration with it, and the image has no PyTorch or TensorFlow to run one.
# Accepted until an Alibi Detect release allows transformers 5 (0.13.0 is still
# the newest on 2026-11-07).
# Remote code from a crafted config.json in from_pretrained(): the job loads no model.
CVE-2026-4372 exp:2027-01-31
# Code execution while initialising a LightGlue model: the job loads no model.
CVE-2026-5241 exp:2027-01-31
# Path traversal in save_pretrained() through chat template names: the job saves nothing with it.
CVE-2026-9856 exp:2027-01-31
